[l_english.EVENT_SUPER_13_NAME]
Die Nebenwelt

[l_english.EVENT_SUPER_13_DESC]
“Neither should we sacrifice the world for one, nor one for the world.”

[l_english.EVENT_SUPER_13_MARK]
Open the Tunnel

[l_english.EVENT_SUPER_13_NEWS_NAME]
Unexpected Encounter

[l_english.EVENT_SUPER_13_NEWS_DESC]
The tunnel slowly opens, and countless Kirins are already standing at the other end of the tunnel. Some saw their long-lost relatives and friends, some saw children who had never existed, and some saw themselves.
They lost this war, but their Nirik fighters earned their compatriots a chance to survive. They crossed the tunnel, took off their thick clothes, and walked from the snowy field to the oasis.
The missing Kirins were also among them. Here, we also met Blossom Burst* and Blossom Burst’, who once bore the stigma of corruption for the entire Kirin commune, but at this moment, they were only proud and relieved.
After them, there was Rain Shine’ who walked while admiring the scenery on both sides of the tunnel: her worst imaginable outcome did not happen, and her efforts were not in vain. She greeted Autumn Blaze* and Rain Shine* who came to meet her, then continued on.
At the end of the refugee line, two Alicorns appeared at the other end of the tunnel - one was pure white with a rainbow-colored mane; the other was deep blue with starry eyes.
“Hello, Autumn Blaze*, I think this is the first time we’ve met. You can call me Celestia.” The white Alicorn said.
“Or more precisely, Celestia-Asterisk.” Rain Shine’ added.

[l_english.EVENT_SUPER_13_NEWS_o]
